        <li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/tutorial-select.html">PostgreSQL 18: querying a table</a> and <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/tutorial-join.html">joins</a> — starting with a statement and following the records into its answer.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/queries-table-expressions.html">Table expressions</a> — matching rows, retaining unmatched rows, and the distinction between join conditions and later filters.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/tutorial-agg.html">Aggregate tutorial</a> and <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/functions-aggregate.html">aggregate functions</a> — grouping, counting, and missing inputs.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/queries-select-lists.html">Select lists and DISTINCT</a> — what output expressions and duplicate removal actually do.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/functions-subquery.html">Subquery expressions</a> — existence tests and their relationship to an outer query.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/libpq-exec.html#LIBPQ-PQEXECPARAMS">Passing query parameters</a> — PostgreSQL’s client-library example of sending values separately from statement text.</li>
